# Known divergence (cosmetic): multigateway rewrites the query before it reaches
# PostgreSQL, so the "LINE 1: ...\n  ^" error-cursor column is offset while the
# error (out-of-range interval) is identical.
#
# Accepted pooling divergence: CREATE FUNCTION pg_temp.f(...) is rejected by
# the gateway (schema-qualified creation into the temporary namespace, see
# temp.patch), so the GROUP_SIZE window-function section errors
# deterministically instead of executing.
